2. In these Regulations —
“authorised person” means —
(a)an officer or employee of the LTA who is authorised under section 43 of the Act for the purposes of these Regulations;
(b)an employee of an operator authorised under section 42AI of the Act to exercise all or any of the powers of an authorised officer under section 42AG(1) of the Act in relation to a public bus or an offence committed or suspected to have been committed under these Regulations; or
(c)a driver of a public bus;
“bicycle” means a two‑wheeled pedal cycle constructed or adapted for use as a means of conveyance, and includes a power‑assisted bicycle;
“double‑decked public bus” means a public bus having 2 decks (one of which is wholly or partly above the other) and each of which is provided with a gangway serving seats on that deck only;
“mobility vehicle” means —
(a)a mobility scooter (as defined by section 2(1) of the Active Mobility Act 2017);
(b)a wheelchair (as defined by section 2(1) of the Active Mobility Act 2017); or
(c)any other motor vehicle prescribed under the Active Mobility Act 2017 for the purpose of paragraph (c) of the definition of “mobility vehicle” in section 2(1) of that Act;
“open pram” or “open stroller” means a pram or stroller that is either —
(a)capable of being folded but is not fully folded; or
(b)designed to not be capable of being folded;
“operator”, in relation to a public bus, means —
(a)if the public bus is operated in the manner described in paragraph (a) of the definition of “public bus” — the public bus operator authorised by a Class 1 bus service licence to operate that public bus;
(b)if the public bus is operated in the manner described in paragraph (b) of the definition of “public bus” — the bus operator authorised by a Class 2 bus service licence to operate that public bus; or
(c)if the public bus is operated in the manner described in paragraph (c) or (d) of the definition of “public bus” — the public bus operator who is operating the bus;
“personal mobility device” and “power‑assisted bicycle” have the meanings given by section 2(1) of the Active Mobility Act 2017;
“public bus” means a bus —
(a)which is —
(i)operated by a public bus operator authorised by a Class 1 bus service licence; and
(ii)operated for the purposes of providing the bus services specified in the public bus services contract between the LTA and that operator;
(b)which is operated by a bus operator for the purposes of providing a temporary bus service to maintain connectivity for passengers during any planned reduced operating hours of a train service, where the provision of that bus service is authorised by a Class 2 bus service licence;
(c)which satisfies all of the following conditions:
(i)the bus is operated by a public bus operator authorised by a Class 1 bus service licence;
(ii)the bus is operated for the purposes of providing alternative transportation for passengers affected by any disruption of a train service; or
(d)which satisfies all of the following conditions:
(i)the bus is operated by a public bus operator authorised by a Class 1 bus service licence;
(ii)the public bus operator is required, pursuant to a contract between the LTA and that operator, to operate a bus service;
(iii)the provision of the bus service mentioned in sub‑paragraph (ii) using the bus is authorised by a Class 2 bus service licence;
(iv)the name of the public bus operator is marked or displayed on the exterior of the bus.

5.—(1) A bus passenger must not bring into a public bus —
(a)any article or thing (other than a mobility vehicle, open pram or open stroller) which —
(i)has dimensions exceeding 120 cm by 70 cm by 40 cm;
(ii)causes, or is likely to cause, any inconvenience, nuisance, obstruction, discomfort or injury to another bus passenger of the public bus;
(iii)causes, or is likely to cause, any damage to the public bus or any property in the public bus; or
(iv)soils, or is likely to soil, the public bus or another bus passenger of, or property in the public bus,
except in accordance with such conditions as may be specified by the LTA or the operator on notices displayed by the LTA or the operator within the public bus; or
(b)any bicycle or personal mobility device.
(2) Despite paragraph (1)(b) but without affecting any other provision in these Regulations, a bus passenger may bring into a public bus a single foldable bicycle or personal mobility device, if —
(a)the foldable bicycle or the personal mobility device (if foldable) is folded and kept folded, with its longest side in a vertical position;
(b)the dimensions of the folded bicycle, personal mobility device or folded personal mobility device (if foldable) do not exceed 120 cm by 70 cm by 40 cm;
(c)if required by an authorised person at the entrance to the public bus — the wheels of the foldable bicycle or personal mobility device are covered so as to prevent any dirt on the wheels being deposited onto the public bus or soiling the dress or clothing of another bus passenger;
(d)if the handlebars or pedals of the foldable bicycle or personal mobility device extend beyond its frame — they are enclosed so as to minimise the risk of injury to any person or damage to any property; and
(e)if the personal mobility device is propelled by an electric motor — the personal mobility device is switched off.
(3) A bus passenger who brings a bicycle or personal mobility device into a public bus pursuant to paragraph (2) must not —
(a)use or ride the bicycle or personal mobility device within the public bus;
(b)leave the bicycle or personal mobility device unattended within the public bus; or
(c)place the bicycle or personal mobility device within the public bus such that it obstructs or impedes the movement of another bus passenger within the public bus.
(4) A person who contravenes paragraph (1) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500.

6.—(1) A bus passenger must not bring a mobility vehicle, open pram or open stroller (each called X) into a public bus unless the following conditions are satisfied:
(a)the length of X does not exceed 120 cm;
(b)the width of X does not exceed 70 cm;
(c)the height does not exceed 150 cm in both of the following circumstances:
(i)when measured vertically from the floor to the topmost part of X;
(ii)when a bus passenger is seated on X — when measured vertically from the floor to the topmost part of the bus passenger’s head;
(d)the total weight of X together with any passenger seated on X must not exceed 300 kilograms.
(2) A person who contravenes paragraph (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500.

12.—(1) A bus passenger, while on a double‑decked public bus, must not —
(a)bring any pram or stroller, bicycle or personal mobility device to the upper deck of the double‑decked public bus;
(b)place any pram or stroller, bicycle or personal mobility device on the staircase leading to the upper deck of the double‑decked public bus;
(c)sit on the staircase leading to the upper deck of the double‑decked public bus; or
(d)stand on the upper deck, or the staircase leading to the upper deck, of the double‑decked public bus unless there is a reasonable excuse for the bus passenger to do so.
(2) A person who contravenes paragraph (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500.
